{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795427544,"nonce":"qa3r6xRkl87loAM08VtQBYuQ3AQ=","message":"Landed in 1523fe13. The mark loop scans up to 16 grey objects per round and prefetches the line of each heap object it finds.\n\nCause found: one list is a chain of dependent loads, so it costs one memory latency per node whatever the loop does. On the Mac retain1 marks at about 95 ns for each node, which is one DRAM miss. The multi-thread row has four such chains, and the old loop finished one before it began the next. Scanning a window of grey objects overlaps the misses of independent chains.\n\nRelease builds, interleaved runs, median of 10 (rows) or of 7 collections (graph shapes).\n\nNUC x86_64, sum of mark ms and wall:\n- retain, 4 threads: mark 1191 to 375 ms, wall 1.78 to 0.97 s\n- trees, 4 threads: mark 78.5 to 63.6 ms, wall 0.154 to 0.141 s\n- retain1, 1 thread: 34.4 to 33.4 ms (unchanged)\n- mark_speed, collect median in ms, base to new: 4w/2p shuffled 173 to 105, 8w/3p shuffled 102 to 79, 4w/2p local 133 to 75, 8w/3p local 88 to 58, 2w/1p local 206 to 98\n\nMac arm64:\n- retain, 4 threads: mark 1412 to 345 ms, wall 1.98 to 0.88 s\n- retain1: 62 to 57 ms (unchanged)\n- mark_speed: 4w/2p shuffled 145 to 65, 8w/3p shuffled 87 to 48, 4w/2p local 110 to 47, 8w/3p local 74 to 35, 2w/1p local 185 to 65\n\nWindow of 8, 16 and 32 differ by under 10%; 16 was kept. The prefetch alone, without the window, gave 10 to 25% on the graph shapes and nothing on the rows.\n\nNot fixed: a single long list still costs one latency per node, so retain1 stays at 3 ms for each MB on the NUC. Fewer collections while the live set is small (3bbb229) is the lever for that row. A mark by several threads would divide the chains further and is not started.\n\nChecks: immix_heap tests (22, including a new fan-out test that fails when the window drops an entry), thread_plugin_collect, band_pool_collect and krio_adapter fiber_collect pass; clippy -D warnings on zyntax_compiler is clean.","files":null}]}